{"decision":"offer_alternatives","reasons":["Moose is on file (large dog).","Rabies and DHPP are valid for the stay.","Bordetella expired 2026-11-14 (before the March 2027 stay), so the vaccine check is not compliant.","A large kennel is free for Mar 10-13 (L2), so the dates work once vaccines are updated."],"reply":"Hi J. Whitfield — thanks for the request to board Moose from March 10 through March 13. Good news: we have a large kennel free for those nights.

The one snag is Moose's vaccinations. His rabies (valid until Jan 23, 2029) and DHPP (valid until Aug 27, 2027) are both fine, but his bordetella expired on Nov 14, 2026, which is before the stay. We can't confirm boarding while bordetella is out of date.

If you can send us an updated bordetella certificate (a recent administration with a valid-until date covering March 10-13, 2027), we'll be able to lock in the booking for those dates — the kennel is available. Just reply with the updated shot record and I'll finalize it for you."}

{"decision": "offer_alternatives", "reasons": ["Olive is on file as a cat.", "A cat-size kennel (C1) is free for the requested March 10-13 boarding stay.", "Vaccine check returned needs_review: rabies is OK, but the FVRCP record on file has no expiry date, so vaccines are not compliant.", "No certificate image was received with the request.", "The issue is fixable by supplying an updated FVRCP vaccine record."], "reply": "Hi! Thanks for your request for Olive to board March 10-13. Good news: we have a cat kennel free for those dates.

However, we can't finalize just yet. Our records show Olive's rabies vaccine is current, but the FVRCP vaccine on file is missing an expiry date, so it doesn't pass our check — and no certificate photo came through with your message.

Could you send an updated vaccine certificate showing Olive's FVRCP details (administration date and expiry)? Once we have that, we can confirm the March 10-13 stay right away. If your plans shift, just let us know and we can look at other dates too."}

